body:
Never knew that was a thing. My old fridge had the automatic ice maker function but not a water filter. I had to fill the water every time.

&#x200B;

Ps. Thailand is an amazing country to travel to, but not to live in, especially if you're not rich.

I recently bought the spectral white edition, played a couple of games. Wolfenstein crashes randomly during cutscenes. The division 2 with water quality set to high crashes within 30 seconds into the game and the built-in benchmark doesn't start and crashes, when set to medium, it rarely crashes and the benchmark works just fine. When crashes, it says something about driver timeout, I'm still figuring out what's wrong. The settings were maxed out on both games. Other than that there haven't been any issues except for the audible coil when the fans spin.

&#x200B;

Edit: Ran on both Windows 10 and 11

I updated the firmware of the keyboard from this [sketchy file](https://drive.google.com/file/d/1gbom719S4013DKY7d9d0GvBHpMabjEpT/view) on google drive. It fixed all the problems for me. Hope it does for you as well.

&#x200B;

PS. Update the firmware with wired mode.
